          "case_name": "In re A.J.C.",
          "citation": "2018 MT 234, 393 Mont. 9, 427 P.3d 59",
          "court": "Montana Supreme Court",
          "year": 2018,
          "date_decided": "2018-09-18",
          "holding": "Reversed: once the father completed his court-ordered treatment plan, the district court unconstitutionally violated his fundamental right to parent by permanently placing the child with the maternal grandmother, a nonparent, and denying him placement; the abuse and neglect proceeding should have been dismissed at that point.",
          "relevance": "It is the leading Montana case on when a dependency case must be dismissed and any remaining custody dispute left to the parenting-plan action.",
          "quote": "At that time, this proceeding should have been dismissed, leaving further consideration of the parenting relationship and parenting plan establishment in the DR matter.",
          "url": "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/6657301/in-re-ajc/",
          "courtlistener_cluster_id": 6657301
        },
        {
          "case_name": "In re D.H.",
          "citation": "2022 MT 37",
          "court": "Montana Supreme Court",
          "year": 2022,
          "date_decided": "2022-02-22",
          "holding": "The district court did not err in dismissing the abuse and neglect proceeding after the child was returned to the custodial mother in South Carolina; the court properly exercised emergency jurisdiction, which ended with the return, and any procedural irregularities did not prejudice the father, whose parental rights remained intact.",
          "relevance": "It is the Montana decision on dismissing a dependency case once the emergency that supported jurisdiction has passed.",
          "quote": "This further investigation when objective concerns regarding the safety of the non-custodial parent are raised during the initial investigation is required.",
          "url": "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/6444484/matter-of-dh-yinc/",
          "courtlistener_cluster_id": 6444484
        }
